<title>USA: University of Colorado $40 mln certificates priced.</title>
<headline>University of Colorado $40 mln certificates priced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>AG Edwards &amp; Sons Inc said Tuesday it tentatively priced $40 million of Regents of the University of Colorado master lease purchase agreement refunding certificates of participation for telecommunications and cogeneration projects, Series 1996, with a top yield of 5.10 percent.</p>
<p>The bonds are AMBAC insured.  </p>
<p>THE REGENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY OF COLORADO</p>
<p>RE: $40,200,000*</p>
<p>MASTER LEASE PURCHASE AGREEMENT REFUNDING</p>
<p>CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION (TELECOMMUNICATIONS</p>
<p>AND COGENERATION PROJECTS) SERIES 1996</p>
<p>MOODY'S: Aaa / A2	    S&amp;P: AAA / A</p>
<p>AMBAC INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 11/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 06/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>12/01/1997		4,195M    4.50  %	  3.80</p>
<p>					  (Approx. $ Price 100.697)</p>
